{"type":"message","id":"fce731ed","parentId":"ea3d2cde","timestamp":"2026-04-08T00:40:15.836Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The API supports pagination with `since_id` and when you pass the last `next_cursor` as `since_id`, you get the next batch of older notes! This confirms that:\n- `since_id=1873611189678932616` gives notes from around 2025-04-18\n- The notes are in reverse chronological order (newest first)\n- We can access older notes by using the `next_cursor` from the previous batch as `since_id`\n- Total notes: 7389\n\nSo the remaining notes to scan are from before 2025-04-12 (the oldest note in the current batch). With 7389 total and we've scanned up to note ID ~1873610563687427488 (2025-04-18), we need to go back much further.\n\n\nNow I'm going to run a scan script that pages backward from cursor `1873611189678932616` to collect all the remaining notes. Since yesterday's quota was already at 796/1000 and we've used more today, I'll be mindful of the limits. Let me first check what the daily quota status looks like.","thinkingSignature":"cc003693019baa2c9bd43f9241929cb572012967245cdef630dda0d87cd67b81"},{"type":"text","text":"找到了！`since_id` 传旧 cursor 可以获取更早的笔记。让我检查今天配额还剩多少：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_kto3ms91unoq_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://openapi.biji.com/open/api/v1/resource/note/list?since_id=1873076662745312464\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: gk_live_79414cc5d34021a6.f48b009c9ed9470d05fbec8f4ef919f4d657e7a15d91347a\" \\\n  -H \"X-Client-ID: cli_a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef90\" 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport sys, json, re\ntext = sys.stdin.read()\nsafe = re.sub(r'\\\"(id|note_id|next_cursor|parent_id|follow_id|live_id)\\\"\\s*:\\s*(\\d+)', r'\\\"\\1\\\":\\\"\\2\\\"', text)\ntry:\n    d = json.loads(safe)\n    notes = d.get('data', {}).get('notes', [])\n    has_more = d.get('data', {}).get('has_more', 'N/A')\n    next_cursor = d.get('data', {}).get('next_cursor', 'N/A')\n    print(f'Has more: {has_more}')\n    print(f'Next cursor: {next_cursor}')\n    print(f'Notes in batch: {len(notes)}')\n    if notes:\n        print(f'Oldest: {notes[-1].get(\\\"id\\\")} | {notes[-1].get(\\\"created_at\\\")}')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'Error: {e}')\n    print(text[:300])\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":42128,"output":625,"cacheRead":40516,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":83269,"cost":{"input":0.0126384,"output":0.00075,"cacheRead":0.00243096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01581936}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775608792519,"responseId":"0624d6d8ecbd70e3e3b4f82f4e83c69c"}}
