{"type":"message","id":"45d5a21e","parentId":"bfd18c57","timestamp":"2026-04-08T10:10:02.556Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tool is rejecting my update because it says \"fields: must be object\". But I'm passing it as an object... Let me check the format more carefully.\n\nLooking at the create action earlier that worked:\n```\n{\"fields\": {\"学科\": \"物理\", \"题目内容\": \"...\", ...}}\n```\n\nFor update, it should be the same format. But the tool is saying fields must be object. Let me try without the record_id parameter since maybe that's causing confusion, or let me look at the tool definition again.\n\nActually looking at the tool definition:\n```\n\"record_id\": {\"description\": \"记录 ID\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n\"fields\": {\"description\": \"记录字段（单条记录）。键为字段名，值根据字段类型而定\", \"type\": \"object\"}\n```\n\nSo `fields` should be a plain object. But it's saying it received a string. This seems like the tool is receiving the stringified version of my JSON instead of the parsed object. This might be a formatting issue with how I'm passing the parameters.\n\nLet me try passing fields as a proper object without any special formatting. The issue might be that my dict with newlines in string values is causing problems when serialized to JSON.\n\nLet me simplify the错因分析 text.","thinkingSignature":"5f382b0946240ef1ecd7443158d032f7db5690f920d8c403f4efeaa81c737197"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ireh9pcew327_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"update","app_token":"TAxUbXUmKaXVuXsNWOacbP1Tne1","table_id":"tblJ7fKHxchaECKz","fields":{"错因分析":"【核心突破：割补法】(1)p相等，h甲小于h乙，所以ρ甲大于ρ乙 (2)割补法：底部p×S=压力=重力，核心直筒部分甲乙重力相等 (3)凸出大肚子部分：体积相同，ρ甲大于ρ乙，所以甲的大肚子部分质量更大 (4)结论：核心相等+附加部分甲更重→甲总质量大于乙","正确答案":"A"},"record_id":"recvgbYdSk2uhV"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":101497,"output":468,"cacheRead":40516,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":142481,"cost":{"input":0.030449